From 1e8cfb36cd141f0eb8516138f1ebb09a4027b5bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:36:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): opt-in queue-fairness evidence capture and live
 report [daveey]

Why: t_9791ec808c66123a asks for measured ready-wait numbers from the live board (p0 median <= 30 min, no card past 120 min while claims happen, alarm and land-turn owner cards claimed <= 10 min). Nothing durable records when a card became ready and when it was claimed across gateways, so none of the three can be read back. This is Phase A of the card's implementation brief v2 (the ordering comparison, Phase B, is not built).

What: scripts/kanban_fairness.py arms a bounded SQLite change journal (kanban_fairness_* tables and triggers, with an opening snapshot, in one transaction) on one Kanban database, drains it to hashed JSONL segments, seals it with a manifest, and reports cohorts and the four gates with interval bounds. A gate passes only on its upper bound, fails only on its lower bound, and is INDETERMINATE for an empty cohort, an unbounded episode, a dropped change, a missing seal, a replaced journal or missing owner history. An inventory command lists flat-1000 producers and alarm keys in named trees and refuses an unclassified match.

No scheduler behaviour changes: nothing in the dispatcher reads the journal, and it does nothing until an operator arms it. kanban_admission_score only gains the ALARM_KEY_PREFIXES name for the tuple it already used.

Not in this commit: the owner_authority.jsonl writer (state repository; until it exists the owner gate reads INDETERMINATE), a per-creation explicit/inherited priority receipt, fleet roster capture, and any measurement window. Trigger cost on a busy board is not measured.

Proof: scripts/run_tests.sh on the four new test files plus tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_urgency_floor.py: 56 passed. The vertical test drives real dispatch_once on a real board database through journal, segments, seal and the CLI report, and checks that the dispatcher's row and event lifecycle is the same with the journal armed and without it. scripts/check: 21 checks ok.
